<title>UK: Glaxo Wellcome says Sweden approves Naramig.</title>
<headline>Glaxo Wellcome says Sweden approves Naramig.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>British pharmaceuticals group Glaxo Wellcome Plc said on Tuesday that Sweden's Medical Products Agency had given the approval to market Naramig, a treatment for migraine.</p>
<p>Glaxo said Sweden was the first country to grant regulatory approval for Naramig and Sweden would act as the reference member state under the European Commission's mutual recognition procedure.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
